 Money lessons for little ones


 


 




 Teaching kids financial literacy can help them build good habits they’ll use for life. Our range of tools and tips makes learning about money fun and easy, showing kids the importance of budgeting, saving and using they money wisely.


 

https://click.mail01.hsbc.co.uk/? 
Visit the learning hub




 

 
 

 
 
 
 


 
 

 
 
 

 
 
 
 
 

 
 
 
 

 
 




 

 
 

 
 
 
 


 
 







 
 

 
 
 
 
 

 
 
 
 
 
 
 


 

 
 
 
 




 Helping Shelter break the cycle of homelessness


 

 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 We're proud to have partnered with homelessness charity Shelter since 2018. Over 1,000 people reach out to Shelter's emergency housing helpline every day, it's a cause that's close to our hearts. And through our support of the 'No Fixed Address' service, we've already helped more than 5,000 people without a fixed address to open bank accounts and rebuild their lives after experiencing homelessness.
 



 

https://click.mail01.hsbc.co.uk/? 
Our work with Shelter





 
 
 
 

 
 
 
 


 

 
 
 
 




 Giving everyone a Safe Space


 

 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 At HSBC we care about protecting our customers. That's why all our branches are Safe Spaces, officially recognised by domestic abuse campaign UK Says No More. If anyone is facing financial or domestic abuse, they can find support and privacy with us to take back control. We'll also connect these people to further resources like domestic abuse helplines and services who can continue to help.

https://click.mail01.hsbc.co.uk/? 
